@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> L

@*
    What a list says when it holds rows but the search and filters match none of
    them. Three of the four lists said nothing at all: a table header, no rows,
    and no explanation — measured on the published site by typing something that
    occurs nowhere. A screen reader read the column titles and then stopped.

    role="status" rather than a plain paragraph, because the reader is typing in a
    search box and will not go looking: the sentence has to come to them. It sits
    below the toolbar on purpose, so the search box that produced this is still
    there to be cleared.
*@
<div class="empty-state small" role="status">
    <p>@(Message ?? L["List_NoMatches"])</p>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Overrides the general sentence where a list can say something better.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Message { get; set; }
}
